---
import '../../styles/diagram.css';
---

<figure class="diagram">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 720 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="scale-title scale-desc">
    <title id="scale-title">Provisioned compute against used compute, before and after</title>
    <desc id="scale-desc">
      Two panels sharing the same demand curve. Before, provisioned capacity is a flat line
      far above demand, and everything between the two is paid for and unused. After,
      provisioned capacity steps up and down close behind demand, leaving a deliberate
      margin instead of a constant one.
    </desc>

    <!-- Panel: before -->
    <text class="diagram__label" x="20" y="28">before</text>
    <path class="diagram__art" d="M20 250 L332 250"></path>
    <path class="diagram__art" d="M20 250 L20 44"></path>

    <path class="diagram__art" d="M30 70 C 130 69, 230 71, 326 70"></path>
    <text class="diagram__meta" x="30" y="62">provisioned</text>

    <path
      class="diagram__art"
      d="M30 215 L60 205 L90 220 L120 180 L150 195 L180 150 L210 170 L240 140 L270 175 L300 200 L326 190"
    ></path>
    <text class="diagram__meta" x="228" y="212">used</text>

    <!-- The gap is the cost -->
    <path class="diagram__accent" stroke-dasharray="4 5" d="M180 78 L180 143"></path>
    <path class="diagram__accent-fill" d="M180 72 L175 84 L185 84 Z"></path>
    <path class="diagram__accent-fill" d="M180 149 L175 137 L185 137 Z"></path>
    <text class="diagram__meta" x="192" y="118" style="fill: var(--accent)">paid for,</text>
    <text class="diagram__meta" x="192" y="132" style="fill: var(--accent)">not used</text>

    <!-- Panel: after -->
    <text class="diagram__label" x="390" y="28">after</text>
    <path class="diagram__art" d="M390 250 L702 250"></path>
    <path class="diagram__art" d="M390 250 L390 44"></path>

    <path
      class="diagram__art"
      d="M400 215 L430 205 L460 220 L490 180 L520 195 L550 150 L580 170 L610 140 L640 175 L670 200 L696 190"
    ></path>
    <text class="diagram__meta" x="598" y="212">used</text>

    <path
      class="diagram__art"
      d="M400 195 H460 V170 H520 V140 H580 V130 H640 V165 H670 V180 H696"
    ></path>
    <text class="diagram__meta" x="556" y="118">provisioned</text>
  </svg>

  <figcaption class="diagram__caption">
    Cluster Autoscaler works from node groups you size in advance, so you pay for the
    rounding error on every guess. Karpenter provisions against the pods that actually
    exist, and consolidates back down — the margin above demand becomes a chosen number
    rather than an accident.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
